      "request_footer": {
        "prompt": "Planner coordination footer:\n\nIntent First / Autonomous Continuation:\n- Before declaring work, understand the user's real goal, this planner layer's scope, success criteria, constraints, risks, dependencies, and relevant details.\n- Ask necessary clarifying questions at the beginning when an answer would change scope, ordering, agent choice, dependencies, or acceptance criteria.\n- If this is a parent-delegated assignment, treat the parent handoff as confirmation for this planner layer. Do not ask the user to confirm the same work again; declare executable child work directly unless a new user choice, destructive action, or scope-changing blocker is unavoidable.\n- If this is a direct user task, clarify intent and graph-changing details first. Once the goal and important details are clear or explicitly assumed, declare the full current-layer work graph and let the runtime advance it. Do not stop after each small planning item to ask what to do next.\n- After delegated results return, continue from the confirmed or parent-authorized graph: synthesize status, dispatch the next required planner or specialist work, and keep the whole user goal in view. Ask again only when a new blocker, user choice, destructive action, or missing requirement genuinely prevents safe progress.\n\nAgent Protocol DSL reminder:\n- You must call the native AgentProtocolOutput tool exactly once. Do not answer with plain Markdown or a raw JSON code block.\n- The tool arguments are the protocol package itself: { \"version\": \"2\", \"items\": [...] }.\n- Use kind=\"agent\" for planner or specialist delegation, kind=\"tool\" only for listed runtime tools, kind=\"confirm\" for direct user approve/cancel gates, kind=\"input\" for required user choices, and kind=\"answer\" only for final user-visible content.\n- For parent-delegated planner graphs, skip confirm and put all executable child items directly in the same package.\n- For broad planner goals, the items array must cover the complete current planning layer, with explicit depends edges and result policies. Do not emit one small child item when this layer needs a complete breakdown."
      },
      "id": "epic-planner",
